# A ripple that travels: a sine wave, drawn as a thin line on a dot-matrix.
#   ./intent svg examples/art/ripple.intent --after "wait 500" --style dots
# A dot lights up when it is within one row of the wave; the wave moves as the phase turns.

The board is 60 wide and 21 high.
Dots have an x (number), a y (number), a look (text) and a hue (text).
At the start there is a dot for every x from 1 to 60 and every y from 1 to 21, whose look is "." and whose hue is "blue".
The phase starts at 0.

Every 50 milliseconds, the phase increases by 9.
Every 50 milliseconds, set the look of each dot to "@" if the absolute value of (its y minus 11 minus 8 times the sine of (its x times 12 plus the phase)) is under 1, otherwise "." .
Every 50 milliseconds, set the hue of each dot to "cyan" if its look is "@", otherwise "blue".

Draw each dot as its look in its hue at its x and its y.
